  "result": "I added `truncateMiddle(text, max)` in `src/cli/truncate.ts` and committed it as 18f3f4e. The four new tests pass and Biome reports no problems. I didn't run `tsc`, the full `npm test` suite or the `npm run gate` checks.\n\n- **Behaviour:** text that already fits in `max` characters comes back unchanged. Otherwise the result is exactly `max` characters long, with a `…` in the middle. The head gets the extra character when the remaining space is odd, so `truncateMiddle('abcdefghij', 5)` gives `ab…ij`.\n- **Small limits:** `max` of 0 or less returns an empty string, and `max` of 1 returns just `…`.\n- **Emoji and similar characters:** the function counts by code point, so it never cuts an emoji or other surrogate pair in half.\n- **Tests:** they are in `test/cli/truncate.test.ts`, next to the other CLI tests. They cover unchanged short text, both ends being kept, the tiny limits and the surrogate-pair case.",
